            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"the-file-cms-hospital-general-information\">The file: CMS <em>Hospital General Information</em></h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">One row per hospital: <strong>5,419 hospitals</strong> across <strong>56</strong> states and territories.\nEach has a type (acute care, critical access, psychiatric, \u2026), an ownership, and a CMS\n<strong>overall star rating</strong> from 1 to 5.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">One thing to notice before you chart anything: <strong>2,245 of 5,419 hospitals\n(41%) have no star rating</strong> \u2014 the file says \"Not Available\". A chart that quietly\ndrops those hospitals tells a different story from one that shows them. In this course they are\nalways shown as their own category.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
